('57a8af92-0b7d-42ba-b5bd-0169d1f9a703', 'assistant', 'Awesome 😄 Let’s upgrade our **Whack-a-Mole** game with **animations** and **sound effects** so it feels more fun!  

We’ll:
- Animate the mole “popping” in and out.
- Play a sound when the mole is hit.
- Add a start/restart button.

---

### **Upgraded Whack-a-Mole with Animations & Sound**

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect, useRef } from ''react'';
import popSoundFile from ''./pop.mp3''; // <-- add your sound file in src folder

function WhackAMole() {
  const [molePosition, setMolePosition] = useState(null);
  const [score, setScore] = useState(0);
  const [timeLeft, setTimeLeft] = useState(0);
  const [isPlaying, setIsPlaying] = useState(false);
  
  const soundRef = useRef(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isPlaying) return;

    // Show mole at random position every 800ms
    const moleInterval = setInterval(() => {
      setMolePosition(Math.floor(Math.random() * 9)); // 9 holes
    }, 800);

    return () => clearInterval(moleInterval);
  }, [isPlaying]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (!isPlaying) return;
    if (timeLeft <= 0) {
      setIsPlaying(false);
      return;
    }
    const timer = setInterval(() => {
      setTimeLeft((t) => t - 1);
    }, 1000);

    return () => clearInterval(timer);
  }, [timeLeft, isPlaying]);

  const hitMole = (index) => {
    if (index === molePosition && isPlaying) {
      setScore((s) => s + 1);
      setMolePosition(null);
      if (soundRef.current) {
        soundRef.current.currentTime = 0;
        soundRef.current.play();
      }
    }
  };

  const startGame = () => {
    setScore(0);
    setTimeLeft(20); // 20 seconds game time
    setIsPlaying(true);
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ textAlign: ''center'', marginTop: ''30px'' }}>
      <h1>🐹 Whack-a-Mole Game</h1>
      <p>Score: {score} | Time Left: {timeLeft}s</p>

      {!isPlaying && (
        <button 
          onClick={startGame} 
          style={{
            padding: ''10px 20px'', 
            fontSize: ''16px'', 
            cursor: ''pointer''
          }}
        >
          Start Game
        </button>
      )}

      <div
        style={{
          display: ''grid'',
          gridTemplateColumns: ''repeat(3, 100px)'',
          gridGap: ''10px'',
          justifyContent: ''center'',
          marginTop: ''20px''
        }}
      >
        {Array.from({ length: 9 }).map((_, index) => (
          <div
            key={index}
            onClick={() => hitMole(index)}
            style={{
              width: ''100px'',
              height: ''100px'',
              backgroundColor: ''#ccc'',
              borderRadius: ''10px'',
              cursor: ''pointer'',
              position: ''relative'',
              overflow: ''hidden''
            }}
          >
            {index === molePosition && (
              <div
                style={{
                  width: ''80px'',
                  height: ''80px'',
                  backgroundColor: ''brown'',
                  borderRadius: ''50%'',
                  position: ''absolute'',
                  bottom: ''0'',
                  left: ''10px'',
                  animation: ''popUp 0.3s ease''
                }}
              />
            )}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <audio ref={soundRef} src={popSoundFile} preload="auto" />

      <style>
        {`
          @keyframes popUp {
            0% { transform: translateY(100%); }
            100% { transform: translateY(0); }
          }
        `}
      </style>

      {!isPlaying && score > 0 && (
        <h2>🎯 Game Over! Final Score: {score}</h2>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}

export default WhackAMole;
```

---

### **Steps to Use**
1. **Get a pop sound effect** (e.g. `pop.mp3`) — you can find free ones on [freesound.org](https://freesound.org) or any free sound site.
2. Place `pop.mp3` in your **`src`** folder.
3. Update the `import popSoundFile from ''./pop.mp3'';` line with the correct file path if needed.
4. Add this code in `WhackAMole.js`.
5. Import and render `<WhackAMole />` in `App.js`.
6. Run:
   ```bash
   npm start
   ```

---

✅ Now, when you start the game:
- Moles pop up with animation.
- Clicking them plays a fun “pop” sound.
- Timer runs for 20 seconds.
- After the game, you can restart easily.

---

