('dbd54d8f-adc4-4190-abe7-270cc7c0a1b5', 'assistant', 'It looks like you''ve shared the beginning of a component called `ChatInterface` using React, MUI, and some custom logic (like API calls and markdown rendering), but the code is truncated.

If you need help with a specific part, please clarify!  
If you want a simple working chat interface template using Material-UI (MUI), here’s a basic version you can adapt:

---

**Basic Chat Interface Example:**

```jsx
import React, { useState } from "react";
import {
  Box,
  Button,
  Typography,
  TextField,
  List,
  ListItem,
  Paper,
} from "@mui/material";

export default function ChatInterface() {
  const [input, setInput] = useState("");
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState([]);

  const handleSend = () => {
    if (!input.trim()) return;
    setMessages([...messages, { text: input, sender: "user" }]);
    setInput("");
    // You could call API here and append bot response to messages
  };

  return (
    <Box
      sx={{
        width: 400,
        mx: "auto",
        mt: 4,
        p: 2,
        bgcolor: "background.paper",
        borderRadius: 2,
        boxShadow: 2,
      }}
    >
      <Typography variant="h6" gutterBottom>
        Chat Interface
      </Typography>
      <Paper variant="outlined" sx={{ p: 1, mb: 2, minHeight: 200 }}>
        <List>
          {messages.map((msg, idx) => (
            <ListItem key={idx}>
              <strong>{msg.sender}: </strong>
              {msg.text}
            </ListItem>
          ))}
        </List>
      </Paper>
      <TextField
        value={input}
        onChange={e => setInput(e.target.value)}
        fullWidth
        placeholder="Type your message..."
        onKeyDown={e => {
          if (e.key === "Enter") handleSend();
        }}
        sx={{ mb: 1 }}
      />
      <Button
        variant="contained"
        onClick={handleSend}
        fullWidth
        disabled={!input.trim()}
      >
        Send
      </Button>
    </Box>
  );
}
```

---

**Key Features:**
- Uses Material-UI (`@mui/material`) for basic styling
- Handles text input and message listing
- Adds new user messages on send; you can plug in your API logic where commented

