('1cb5a9ef-19f1-4e82-bb4d-2e89d0bafe84', 'assistant', 'Of course! Here’s a simple calculator app example in **Angular**. This code covers basic operations (addition, subtraction, multiplication, division).

### Step 1: Create an Angular App

If you haven’t already, create a new Angular project:

```bash
ng new calculator-app
cd calculator-app
ng serve
```

### Step 2: Create a Calculator Component

Generate a calculator component:

```bash
ng generate component calculator
```

### Step 3: Add Calculator Code

#### 1. **calculator.component.ts**

```typescript
import { Component } from ''@angular/core'';

@Component({
  selector: ''app-calculator'',
  templateUrl: ''./calculator.component.html'',
  styleUrls: [''./calculator.component.css'']
})
export class CalculatorComponent {
  input: string = '''';
  result: string = '''';

  append(value: string) {
    this.input += value;
  }

  clear() {
    this.input = '''';
    this.result = '''';
  }

  calculate() {
    try {
      // Use Function for evaluation, but be aware it''s not safe for untrusted input
      // For production, use a math library like math.js
      // eslint-disable-next-line no-new-func
      this.result = new Function(''return '' + this.input)().toString();
    } catch (e) {
      this.result = ''Error'';
    }
  }
}
```

#### 2. **calculator.component.html**

```html
<div class="calculator">
  <input type="text" [value]="input" readonly />
  <div class="result" *ngIf="result">Result: {{ result }}</div>
  <div class="buttons">
    <button (click)="append(''1'')">1</button>
    <button (click)="append(''2'')">2</button>
    <button (click)="append(''3'')">3</button>
    <button (click)="append(''+'')">+</button>
    <br />
    <button (click)="append(''4'')">4</button>
    <button (click)="append(''5'')">5</button>
    <button (click)="append(''6'')">6</button>
    <button (click)="append(''-'')">-</button>
    <br />
    <button (click)="append(''7'')">7</button>
    <button (click)="append(''8'')">8</button>
    <button (click)="append(''9'')">9</button>
    <button (click)="append(''*'')">*</button>
    <br />
    <button (click)="append(''0'')">0</button>
    <button (click)="append(''.'')">.</button>
    <button (click)="clear()">C</button>
    <button (click)="append(''/'')">/</button>
    <br />
    <button (click)="calculate()" style="width: 100%">=</button>
  </div>
</div>
```

#### 3. **calculator.component.css** (optional)

```css
.calculator {
  max-width: 250px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  padding: 20px;
  border: 1px solid #ccc;
  border-radius: 8px;
  background: #f9f9f9;
}

input {
  width: 90%;
  font-size: 1.2em;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  text-align: right;
  padding: 5px;
}

.result {
  font-weight: bold;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
}

.buttons button {
  width: 40px;
  height: 40px;
  margin: 3px;
  font-size: 1.2em;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

### Step 4: Use the Calculator Component

Update `app.component.html` to use your new calculator:

```html
<app-calculator></app-calculator>
```

---

**Now you have a basic calculator app in Angular!**  
You can add more features, styles, or validation as needed. Let me know if you want to add history, scientific functions, or more advanced features!', NULL, 12, 0, 866, '1c09bc27-1da3-4dc9-b90c-103913e2679f', '14178080-b09c-437f-ae9e-ba218d455a6f', NULL, '8cc133c9-d905-468e-9231-6eac185f0e02', '2025-10-03 14:43:40.366000+00:00', '2025-10-03 14:43:40.366000+00:00', FALSE, NULL, NULL),
