('1eae5d91-95f6-4d60-8a5d-4cac10fd6056', 'assistant', 'Great! Creating a calculator app in React.js is a fantastic way to learn the basics. Here’s a step-by-step guide to help you get started:

### Step 1: Set Up Your React App

If you haven''t already, create a new React app using Create React App:

```bash
npx create-react-app calculator-app
cd calculator-app
npm start
```

### Step 2: Create the Calculator Component

Replace the code in `src/App.js` with the following simple calculator code:

```jsx
import React, { useState } from ''react'';
import ''./App.css'';

function App() {
  const [input, setInput] = useState('''');

  const handleClick = (value) => {
    setInput(input + value);
  };

  const handleClear = () => {
    setInput('''');
  };

  const handleEqual = () => {
    try {
      setInput(eval(input).toString());
    } catch {
      setInput(''Error'');
    }
  };

  return (
    <div className="calculator">
      <input type="text" value={input} readOnly />
      <div className="buttons">
        {[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9,0,''.''].map(num => (
          <button key={num} onClick={() => handleClick(num.toString())}>{num}</button>
        ))}
        {[''+'', ''-'', ''*'', ''/''].map(op => (
          <button key={op} onClick={() => handleClick(op)}>{op}</button>
        ))}
        <button onClick={handleClear}>C</button>
        <button onClick={handleEqual}>=</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}

export default App;
```

### Step 3: Add Basic Styles (Optional)

Add some simple styles in `src/App.css` to make it look better:

```css
.calculator {
  width: 250px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  padding: 20px;
  background: #f4f4f4;
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px #ccc;
  text-align: center;
}

input {
  width: 90%;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  font-size: 1.2em;
  padding: 5px;
  text-align: right;
}

.buttons button {
  width: 50px;
  height: 50px;
  margin: 5px;
  font-size: 1.2em;
  cursor: pointer;
}
```

### Step 4: Run Your App

Make sure your app is running with:

```bash
npm start
```

---

**Note:**  
This is a basic calculator. You may want to improve it by handling more complex operations or edge cases, and avoid using `eval()` for security reasons in production apps.

Let me know if you need help with specific features or want to make it more advanced!', NULL, 4, 0, 626, '1c09bc27-1da3-4dc9-b90c-103913e2679f', '14178080-b09c-437f-ae9e-ba218d455a6f', NULL, '8cc133c9-d905-468e-9231-6eac185f0e02', '2025-10-03 11:14:07.241000+00:00', '2025-10-03 11:14:07.241000+00:00', FALSE, NULL, NULL),
