```', NULL, 24, NULL, NULL, '366c8e29-d8cd-4414-bbbc-aa5e6aed75db', '2b12eb8b-49d4-45e1-85f3-f496a9a4883d', '4ea5c16d-561d-4d25-8d4c-867994ccf463', NULL, '2025-10-27 12:44:40.226000+00:00', '2025-10-27 12:44:40.226000+00:00', FALSE, '{"sql":"SELECT \n    m.name AS model_name,\n    SUM(e.tokens_output) * 1.0 / NULLIF(SUM(e.tokens_input), 0) AS token_efficiency\nFROM [AIDD].usage_events e\nJOIN [AIDD].llm_models m ON e.model_id = m.id\nGROUP BY \n    m.name\nORDER BY\n    token_efficiency DESC","is_sql_valid":true,"results":[{"model_name":"[Unserializable str: gpt-4.1]","token_efficiency":"[Unserializable Decimal: 0.461187214611]"}],"mode":"gpt","chat_type":"vanna","explanation":"## Key Patterns & Trends - Token efficiency varies significantly by model, indicating differences in how models generate output relative to input size. - Some models demonstrate higher output per input token, suggesting more concise or information-dense responses. - Lower token efficiency may reflect models that produce longer or more verbose outputs for similar inputs. ## Notable Observations - The model \"gpt-4.1\" has a token efficiency of approximately 0.46, meaning it generates less than half an output token for every input token. - This efficiency rate may be typical for advanced models that prioritize quality, context, and relevance over sheer output length. - Models with higher efficiency could be optimized for tasks requiring more expansive or detailed responses. ## Insights - Token efficiency is a useful metric for evaluating cost-effectiveness, especially in environments with strict token usage limits or pricing based on token consumption. - Models with lower token efficiency may be preferable for tasks that require concise, focused answers. - Conversely, higher efficiency models might be better suited for tasks that need elaboration or comprehensive explanations. ## Business or Operational Implications - Understanding token efficiency helps in selecting the right model for specific business needs, balancing output quality and operational costs. - Organizations can optimize their model usage by choosing models that align with their communication style and cost constraints. - Monitoring token efficiency over time can inform decisions about model upgrades, workflow adjustments, or budgeting for AI-powered operations. "}', 'vanna_response'),
