('a9c2ba0f-a662-4f25-a43d-5f22d9d847dc', 'assistant', 'Got it ✅ — you want the upgraded **Whack-a-Mole game** with animations and sounds all inside a **single React component** file.  
Here’s a complete version you can drop directly into `App.js` and run.

---

### 🎮 Animated Whack-a-Mole Game (Single Component)

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect } from ''react'';

export default function App() {
  const [molePosition, setMolePosition] = useState(null);
  const [score, setScore] = useState(0);
  const [timeLeft, setTimeLeft] = useState(20);
  const moleAppearSound = new Audio(
    "https://www.soundjay.com/buttons/sounds/button-16.mp3"
  );
  const hitSound = new Audio(
    "https://www.soundjay.com/buttons/sounds/button-10.mp3"
  );

  useEffect(() => {
    const moleInterval = setInterval(() => {
      const randomPosition = Math.floor(Math.random() * 9);
      setMolePosition(randomPosition);
      moleAppearSound.play();
    }, 800);

    return () => clearInterval(moleInterval);
  }, []);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (timeLeft <= 0) return;
    const timer = setInterval(() => {
      setTimeLeft((t) => t - 1);
    }, 1000);

    return () => clearInterval(timer);
  }, [timeLeft]);

  const hitMole = (index) => {
    if (index === molePosition) {
      setScore((s) => s + 1);
      setMolePosition(null);
      hitSound.play();
    }
  };

  return (
    <div style={{ textAlign: ''center'', marginTop: ''30px'', fontFamily: ''Arial'' }}>
      <h1 style={{ color: ''#4CAF50'' }}>🐹 Whack-a-Mole Game</h1>
      <p style={{ fontSize: ''18px'' }}>Score: {score} | Time Left: {timeLeft}s</p>

      {timeLeft > 0 ? (
        <div
          style={{
            display: ''grid'',
            gridTemplateColumns: ''repeat(3, 100px)'',
            gridGap: ''10px'',
            justifyContent: ''center'',
            marginTop: ''20px''
          }}
        >
          {Array.from({ length: 9 }).map((_, index) => (
            <div
              key={index}
              onClick={() => hitMole(index)}
              style={{
                width: ''100px'',
                height: ''100px'',
                backgroundColor: ''#ccc'',
                borderRadius: ''10px'',
                cursor: ''pointer'',
                display: ''flex'',
                justifyContent: ''center'',
                alignItems: ''center'',
                boxShadow: ''0 4px 6px rgba(0,0,0,0.1)'',
                position: ''relative'',
                overflow: ''hidden''
              }}
            >
              {index === molePosition && (
                <div
                  style={{
                    width: ''80px'',
                    height: ''80px'',
                    backgroundColor: ''brown'',
                    borderRadius: ''50%'',
                    transition: ''transform 0.2s ease'',
                    transform: ''translateY(0)''
                  }}
                />
              )}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      ) : (
        <h2 style={{ color: ''#f44336'', marginTop: ''20px'' }}>
          ⏳ Game Over! Final Score: {score}
        </h2>
      )}
    </div>
  );
}
```

---

### 🚀 How to Run
1. Create a new React app:
   ```bash
   npx create-react-app whack-a-mole
   cd whack-a-mole
   ```
2. Replace **all contents** of `src/App.js` with the code above.
3. Start the game:
   ```bash
   npm start
   ```

---

### 🔹 Features
- Mole appears randomly every 800ms
- **Sound effects** when mole appears and when you hit it
- Simple animation effect
- Fully contained in **one component** (`App`)

---

