('33ced161-89a0-4757-8125-6ad388409e71', 'assistant', 'It looks like you pasted your ChatInterface component code twice and it cuts off abruptly at the end ("const { conversationId } = usePara"), so it’s incomplete. 

**Here’s how you can clean up and organize your code, and some advice for common issues in React functional components:**

---

## 1. Remove Duplicated Imports and Code

You do not need to import the same libraries and components twice. Also, only one `ChatInterface` function should be exported.

---

## 2. File Structure

Your file should look like:

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect, useRef } from "react";
// MUI Imports...
import { useNavigate, useParams } from "react-router-dom";
// API Imports...
import MarkdownMessage from "../MarkdownMsg/MarkdownMsg";
import SQLMessage from "../MarkdownMsg/SQLMessage";
// Redux
import { useSelector } from "react-redux";

// Function Component
export default function ChatInterface() {
  // Hooks, state, refs, etc...
  // Your logic (fetchConversation, handleNewChat, etc...)

  // Render JSX
  return (
    <Box>
      {/* Your UI here */}
    </Box>
  );
}
```

---

## 3. Incomplete Code Issue

Your second copy is truncated at:
```js
const { conversationId } = usePara
```
Make sure you use:
```js
const { conversationId } = useParams();
```

---

## 4. Clean Up State and Refs

You can organize your state and refs at the top of your component for clarity.

---

## 5. Potential Infinite Fetch Issue

If you have this effect:
```js
useEffect(() => { fetchConversation(); }, [conversationId]);
```
That''s correct! Just ensure you do not accidentally call `setMessages` inside another effect that depends on `messages`, or you''ll risk an infinite loop.

---

## 6. Scroll to Bottom

You have:
```js
useEffect(() => {
  scrollRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth" });
}, [messages, streamingMessage]);
```
That''s good! Just be sure that `scrollRef` is attached to your last message in the JSX.

---

## 7. Show Loading Spinner

If `isInitialLoading` is true, render a spinner at the top of your return JSX.

---

## 8. Copy, Edit, More Menu, etc.

Be sure all handlers (`handleEdit`, `handleCopy`, `handleMenuOpen`, etc.) are implemented, or remove unused code.

---

## 9. Avoid Duplicate Function Names/Components

Don’t define `ChatInterface` twice.

---

## Example Clean Skeleton

```jsx
import React, { useState, useEffect, useRef } from "react";
import { Box, CircularProgress } from "@mui/material";
import { useNavigate, useParams } from "react-router-dom";
// Import other needed components, icons, hooks, services, etc.

export default function ChatInterface() {
  const { conversationId } = useParams();
  const [messages, setMessages] = useState([]);
  const [isInitialLoading, setIsInitialLoading] = useState(false);
  const scrollRef = useRef(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    async function fetchConversation() {
      if (!conversationId) {
        // handleNewChat();
        return;
      }
      setIsInitialLoading(true);
      try {
        const response = await getConversationbyId(conversationId);
        if (response.success && response.messages) {
          setMessages(response.messages.map(/* your transform here */));
        } else {
          setMessages([
            { type: "assistant", text: "Hello! I''m your AI assistant." }
          ]);
        }
      } catch (e) {
        setMessages([
          { type: "assistant", text: "Hello! I''m your AI assistant." }
        ]);
      } finally {
        setIsInitialLoading(false);
      }
    }
    fetchConversation();
  }, [conversationId]);

  useEffect(() => {
    scrollRef.current?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth" });
  }, [messages]);

  return (
    <Box>
      {isInitialLoading ? <CircularProgress /> : null}
      {messages.map((msg, idx) => (
        <Box key={msg.id || idx} ref={idx === messages.length-1 ? scrollRef : null}>
          {/* Render message, e.g. <MarkdownMessage text={msg.text} /> */}
        </Box>
      ))}
      {/* Chat input and actions here */}
    </Box>
  );
}
```

---

