('205d2801-feab-4778-a819-753b90e2cbdd', 'assistant', 'Got it! You want a simple **calculator app** built in **Angular**.  
I’ll give you a step-by-step guide with code so you can set it up quickly.  

---

## **Step 1: Create a New Angular Project**
Make sure you have Angular CLI installed:

```bash
npm install -g @angular/cli
```

Create a new project:

```bash
ng new calculator-app
cd calculator-app
ng serve
```

---

## **Step 2: Create Calculator Component**
```bash
ng generate component calculator
```

---

## **Step 3: Calculator HTML (`calculator.component.html`)**
```html
<div class="calculator">
  <h2>Angular Calculator</h2>

  <input type="text" [(ngModel)]="display" readonly />

  <div class="buttons">
    <button *ngFor="let btn of buttons" (click)="press(btn)">{{ btn }}</button>
    <button class="equal" (click)="calculate()">=</button>
    <button class="clear" (click)="clear()">C</button>
  </div>
</div>
```

---

## **Step 4: Calculator TypeScript (`calculator.component.ts`)**
```typescript
import { Component } from ''@angular/core'';

@Component({
  selector: ''app-calculator'',
  templateUrl: ''./calculator.component.html'',
  styleUrls: [''./calculator.component.css'']
})
export class CalculatorComponent {
  display: string = '''';
  buttons: string[] = [''7'',''8'',''9'',''/'',''4'',''5'',''6'',''*'',''1'',''2'',''3'',''-'',''0'',''.'',''+''];

  press(btn: string) {
    this.display += btn;
  }

  clear() {
    this.display = '''';
  }

  calculate() {
    try {
      this.display = eval(this.display).toString();
    } catch {
      this.display = ''Error'';
    }
  }
}
```
⚠ **Note:** Using `eval()` is fine for a demo but **not safe** for production. In real apps, use a proper math expression parser.

---

## **Step 5: Add Styles (`calculator.component.css`)**
```css
.calculator {
  width: 250px;
  margin: 50px auto;
  padding: 15px;
  background: #f1f1f1;
  border-radius: 10px;
  text-align: center;
}

input {
  width: 100%;
  height: 40px;
  font-size: 18px;
  margin-bottom: 10px;
  text-align: right;
  padding-right: 5px;
}

.buttons {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 5px;
}

button {
  padding: 10px;
  font-size: 18px;
  cursor: pointer;
}

.equal {
  grid-column: span 2;
  background: green;
  color: white;
}

.clear {
  grid-column: span 2;
  background: red;
  color: white;
}
```

---

## **Step 6: Enable Two-way Binding**
In `app.module.ts`, import `FormsModule`:

```typescript
import { NgModule } from ''@angular/core'';
import { BrowserModule } from ''@angular/platform-browser'';
import { FormsModule } from ''@angular/forms'';

import { AppComponent } from ''./app.component'';
import { CalculatorComponent } from ''./calculator/calculator.component'';

@NgModule({
  declarations: [
    AppComponent,
    CalculatorComponent
  ],
  imports: [
    BrowserModule,
    FormsModule
  ],
  providers: [],
  bootstrap: [AppComponent]
})
export class AppModule { }
```

---

## **Step 7: Use Component in App**
In `app.component.html`:

```html
<app-calculator></app-calculator>
```

---

✅ Now run:
```bash
ng serve
```
Open `http://localhost:4200` — you’ll have a working calculator in Angular.

---

