('d2627b08-acfa-41d3-8ddf-a1a5df632d4f', 'assistant', 'Great question! The way my responses appear—aligned to the left or full width—is determined by the platform or application you’re using to interact with me (the AI), not by my code or formatting. My responses are plain text or markdown, and how they’re displayed is controlled by the user interface of your chat client, website, or app.

**If you want your calculator app''s display to be full width (centered or stretched across the screen), you can control that with CSS in your React project.** Here’s how you can make your calculator appear full width or centered:

---

### 1. **Full Width Calculator**

Update your CSS in `App.css`:

```css
.calculator {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 500px; /* Set a max width for large screens */
  margin: 50px auto;
  padding: 20px;
  background: #f4f4f4;
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 0 10px #ccc;
  text-align: center;
}
```

This will make your calculator stretch to the available width (up to 500px), and center it on the page.

---

### 2. **Fully Responsive (100% Width on Mobile and Desktop)**

```css
.calculator {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 100%;
  margin: 0;
  padding: 20px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

You can also use media queries for better responsiveness:

```css
@media (max-width: 600px) {
  .calculator {
    padding: 10px;
    font-size: 1em;
  }
}
```

---

### 3. **Center the Calculator Horizontally and Vertically**

```css
body, html {
  height: 100%;
  margin: 0;
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}

.calculator {
  width: 100%;
  max-width: 400px;
}
```

---

**Summary:**  
- My answer alignment is not controlled by me, but by your platform’s UI.
