('5992c1b6-dfa4-43f3-81ab-a582fa6a8128', 'assistant', 'Great! Here are some ideas for **next steps** to improve or expand your calculator app in React:

---

### 1. Keyboard Support

Allow users to use their keyboard for input.  
Add an event listener for keyboard events and handle them in your component.

**Example:**

```jsx
React.useEffect(() => {
  const handleKeyDown = (e) => {
    if ((e.key >= ''0'' && e.key <= ''9'') || [''+'', ''-'', ''*'', ''/'', ''.''].includes(e.key)) {
      setInput((prev) => prev + e.key);
    }
    if (e.key === ''Enter'') handleEqual();
    if (e.key === ''Escape'') handleClear();
  };
  window.addEventListener(''keydown'', handleKeyDown);
  return () => window.removeEventListener(''keydown'', handleKeyDown);
}, [input]);
```

---

### 2. Expression Validation

Prevent invalid expressions (like `2++3` or `..`).  
You can use a library like [mathjs](https://mathjs.org/) or write basic checks before calculation.

**Example using mathjs:**

```bash
npm install mathjs
```

```jsx
import { evaluate } from ''mathjs'';

const handleEqual = () => {
  try {
    setResult(evaluate(input));
  } catch {
    setResult(''Error'');
  }
};
```

---

### 3. History Feature

Show a list of previous calculations.

```jsx
const [history, setHistory] = useState([]);

const handleEqual = () => {
  try {
    // ... calculation code
    setHistory([...history, { input, result: calculation }]);
  } catch {
    setResult(''Error'');
  }
};

// Render history
{history.map((item, idx) => (
  <div key={idx}>{item.input} = {item.result}</div>
))}
```

---

### 4. Scientific Functions

Add buttons for square root, power, etc.

```jsx
<button onClick={() => handleClick(''Math.sqrt('')}>√</button>
<button onClick={() => handleClick(''**'')}>^</button>
```

You’ll need to update your calculation logic to handle these.

---

### 5. Better UI

Use [Material-UI](https://mui.com/) or [Ant Design](https://ant.design/) for a more polished look.

```bash
npm install @mui/material @emotion/react @emotion/styled
```

---

### 6. Mobile Responsiveness

Make sure your calculator looks good on all devices using CSS media queries or frameworks like Bootstrap.

---

### 7. Deploy Your App

Publish your calculator online using [Vercel](https://vercel.com/), [Netlify](https://netlify.com/), or GitHub Pages.

---

**Let me know which feature you want to try next, and I can give you detailed code or instructions!**', NULL, 8, 0, 604, '1c09bc27-1da3-4dc9-b90c-103913e2679f', '14178080-b09c-437f-ae9e-ba218d455a6f', NULL, '8cc133c9-d905-468e-9231-6eac185f0e02', '2025-10-03 14:36:57.104000+00:00', '2025-10-03 14:36:57.104000+00:00', FALSE, NULL, NULL),
