('fd8b6845-fa03-42e1-b18f-b7dc230df477', 'assistant', '', NULL, 6, NULL, NULL, '1c09bc27-1da3-4dc9-b90c-103913e2679f', 'b372334a-16ba-4095-85dc-a0c0b364172c', 'c67dcb98-71c1-4fea-9104-15dc48795fcd', NULL, '2025-10-30 13:17:24.210000+00:00', '2025-10-30 13:17:24.210000+00:00', FALSE, '{"mode":"gpt","chat_type":"vanna","explanation":"## Key Patterns & Trends - All users listed have an active status and are flagged as active. - The majority of users have verified their email addresses, though a few have not. - Most users do not have company or plan associations; fields are predominantly null. - User roles vary, including \"admin\", \"DB_ADMIN\", \"DATA_ANALYST\", and \"user\". - Many users have missing personal details (first name, last name, display name). - The \"last_login\" field is frequently null, indicating many users have not logged in yet. ## Notable Observations - Only one user (John Doe) has a recorded recent login activity. - Several users have email addresses associated with organizations (e.g., cloudomax.com), suggesting possible business or team usage. - A significant number of users have not provided consent, and profile details such as profile pictures and phone numbers are mostly absent. - The presence of multiple tenant IDs indicates users are distributed across different organizational contexts or environments. ## Insights - User activation is high, but engagement (as measured by login activity) is low for most accounts. - Email verification rates are strong, which is positive for account security and communications. - The lack of personal and company information may indicate either a simplified onboarding process or incomplete user profiles. - Role diversity suggests the system supports both administrative and standard user functions. ## Business or Operational Implications - Consider implementing strategies to encourage user engagement, such as onboarding emails or login reminders. - Encourage users to complete their profiles for better personalization and communication. - Review onboarding and consent processes to ensure compliance and improved data quality. - Monitor inactive but active accounts for potential cleanup or re-engagement campaigns. - The distribution across tenants and roles may require tailored support and documentation for different user groups. ","debugMode":false}', 'vanna_response'),
