### 2. Create Project Folder
Open your terminal and run:
```bash
mkdir my-node-project
cd my-node-project
```

### 3. Initialize Node.js Project
Run:
```bash
npm init -y
```
This creates a `package.json` file with default settings.

### 4. Create Main File
Create a file named `index.js`:
```bash
touch index.js
```

### 5. Write Basic Code
Open `index.js` and add:
```javascript
// index.js
console.log(''Hello, Node.js!'');
```

### 6. Run Your Project
In the terminal, run:
```bash
node index.js
```
You should see:
```
Hello, Node.js!
```

---

**Next Steps:**  
If you want to set up a simple web server, install Express:
```bash
npm install express
```
Then, update `index.js`:
```javascript
const express = require(''express'');
const app = express();

app.get(''/'', (req, res) => {
  res.send(''Hello, Express!'');
});

app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log(''Server running on http://localhost:3000'');
});
```
Run with:
```bash
node index.js
```
Visit `http://localhost:3000` in your browser.

